 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_xrmg2fo",
   "entryDay": 41,
   "cause": "the expedition",
   "lines": [
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Kennedy Santos is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d41: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d41: 🕯️ Kennedy Santos is dead — the expedition. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d41: What Kennedy kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d41: \"Kennedy's gone.\" Carmine looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Kennedy.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d41: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Madison blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Food Preservation (Level 1). Salt, smoke, dry. The big three. Salt draws water out; bacteria can't live without it.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Reading Weather (Level 1). Red sky at night, shepherd's delight. Red sky at morning, shepherd's warning. It works.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Animal Behavior (Level 1). Most animals flee. Give them an escape route and they take it. Cornered animals fight.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Cordage (Level 1). Twist plant fibers into string. Dogbane, nettle, yucca — strong fibers are everywhere.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Reading the Land (Level 1). Eat the landscape with your eyes first: green + water + sun means food grows here. Start where those three meet.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Soft Step (Level 1). Move through woods like weather. Less noise, fewer surprises.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Field Dressing (Level 1). Break down game fast and clean. Less waste, more meat, usable parts.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Reading Tracks (Level 1). Fresh tracks have sharp edges. Old tracks crumble. You can tell how recently something passed.",
    "d41: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Kennedy Santos, 41 days. The mantle passes to Madison Kozlowski.",
    "d41: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Madison Kozlowski, 20 — a farmer. Their hands know different work now: Beast-calm, Lucky Rock.",
    "d41: The village's quarrel was with Kennedy — and Kennedy is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d41: At the grave, Carmine, Yesenia, Ursula and 4 more speak for Madison — \"Kennedy trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d41: The fire knew Madison before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_t4jgq14",
   "entryDay": 62,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d62: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Madison Kozlowski is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d62: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d62: 🕯️ Madison is dead — and the dead hold no treaties. Every link Haven has shakes.",
    "d62: Emberhold watches to see if Haven holds without its dead. The bond is young — they're still deciding what Haven is, and grief delays the verdict. They'll test the link — count on it, unless Haven answers first: send grain (1,500 kcal), send a speaker (2 days), or let the silence answer.",
    "d62: Ashford watches to see if Haven holds without its dead. The bond is young — they're still deciding what Haven is, and grief delays the verdict. They'll test the link — count on it, unless Haven answers first: send grain (1,500 kcal), send a speaker (2 days), or let the silence answer.",
    "d62: Thornfield watches to see if Haven holds without its dead. The bond is young — they're still deciding what Haven is, and grief delays the verdict. They'll test the link — count on it, unless Haven answers first: send grain (1,500 kcal), send a speaker (2 days), or let the silence answer.",
    "d62: 🕯️ Madison Kozlowski is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d62: What Madison kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d62: \"Madison's gone.\" Yesenia looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Madison.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d62: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Meera blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d62: 📖 LEARNED: Steady Hands (Level 1). Fine work under pressure. Dressing game, stitching wounds, tying snares — no shake.",
    "d62: 📖 LEARNED: Patient Aim (Level 1). One shot. You don't take the shot unless it's the shot.",
    "d62: 📖 LEARNED: Wound Care (Level 1). Clean it, close it, cover it. Pressure stops bleeding. Clean water is better than dirty hands.",
    "d62: ⚡ TECHNIQUE UNLOCKED: Precise Mend! Your healing knows where to go. +50% effectiveness. (Your knowledge of Wound Care amplifies your field_medicine.)",
    "d62: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d62: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Madison Kozlowski, 62 days. The mantle passes to Meera Reddy.",
    "d62: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Meera Reddy, 39 — a Dentist. Her hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Beard Moss, Berserker Rage.",
    "d62: The village's quarrel was with Madison — and Madison is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d62: You knew Madison — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting them, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d62: At the grave, Carmine, Yesenia, Ursula and 3 more speak for Meera — \"Madison trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d62: The fire knew Meera before the Codex did — her name already carried weight here."
